design:
The merged index should be deterministic: base records first, add-ons by explicit order, later records accepted only when their `overrides` metadata names the earlier pack/key. Return a typed error such as `RulesPackError` for invalid stacks. Normalize lookup names the same way SRD lookup does today: trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case en-US.

Initial test sketch:
```ts
const stack = resolveRulesStack({ base: basePack(), addons: [addonPack({ order: 10 })] });
expect(lookupRulesRecord(stack, { kind: 'creature', ref: 'creature:goblin' }).ok).toBe(true);
expect(() => resolveRulesStack({ base: basePack(), addons: [addonPack({ records: [record('creature:goblin')] })] })).toThrow(RulesPackError);
```
